---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { link } from '@lib/nav';
---

<BaseLayout title="Editorial Policy" description="How DhanPedia researches, verifies, updates, and refuses to publish.">
  <section style="padding:3rem 0 3rem;">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:48rem;">
      <h1 style="font-size:2rem; margin:0 0 .4rem;">Editorial policy</h1>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.2rem; margin-bottom:.5rem;">Voice & scope</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-soft); line-height:1.75;">
        Rigorous, analytical, neutral, and transparent about uncertainty.
        Beginners are served without oversimplifying for advanced readers.
        Each article answers: what it is, how it works, how returns are generated,
        what can destroy those returns, costs & taxes, eligibility, liquidity,
        evidence, alternatives, common misconceptions, and when it is inappropriate.
      </p>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.2rem; margin-bottom:.5rem;">Source hierarchy</h2>
      <ol style="color:var(--ink-soft); line-height:1.8;">
        <li>Statutes, official gazettes, court decisions</li>
        <li>RBI · SEBI · Income Tax Dept · Ministry of Finance</li>
        <li>AMFI · IRDAI · PFRDA · NSE/BSE · DICGC · Department of Posts</li>
        <li>Official circulars, fund documents, product disclosures</li>
        <li>Company annual reports, audited financials</li>
        <li>Peer-reviewed research, reputable financial publications</li>
        <li>Community discussion — anecdote only, never proof</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.2rem; margin-bottom:.5rem;">What we never do</h2>
      <ul style="color:var(--ink-soft); line-height:1.8;">
        <li>Never promise a return or guarantee capital.</li>
        <li>Never present a yield as a total return without explaining the difference.</li>
        <li>Never compare incompatible time periods, tax assumptions, or risk levels without saying so.</li>
        <li>Never claim "currently available" without current verification.</li>
        <li>Never instruct readers to commit fraud, market manipulation, or any illegal financial activity.</li>
        <li>Never publish a "peer-reviewed" claim unless a review actually happened.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.2rem; margin-bottom:.5rem;">Time-sensitive claims</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-soft); line-height:1.75;">
        Tax rules, rates, limits, eligibility, and availability carry a
        <code>lastVerified</code> date, live in the <a href={link('/sources')}>update register</a>,
        and are re-checked after every Budget and RBI MPC. A continuous-integration
        job may <em>flag</em> items past their review date, but it never auto-publishes
        regulatory changes — editorial approval plus source verification are required.
      </p>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.2rem; margin-bottom:.5rem;">Conflicts & monetization</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-soft); line-height:1.75;">
        DhanPedia takes no payments for recommendations, no sponsored content,
        and no affiliate fees. If a disclosure ever becomes necessary it will be
        stated here and on the relevant page. There are no partnerships,
        endorsements, or regulatory approvals claimed.
      </p>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.2rem; margin-bottom:.5rem;">Regulated vs unregulated</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-soft); line-height:1.75;">
        We clearly separate RBI/SEBI-regulated activity (e.g., NBFC-P2P platforms
        under the 2025 Directions, SEBI PMS/AIFs) from unregistered schemes,
        illegal deposit-taking, and misleading "investment" pitches, and we say
        so plainly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
